<section class="part" id="words">
<h2>Words on this page</h2>
<dl class="gloss">
<dt>coordinator</dt><dd>Main session of the revival. It talks to you, briefs the workers, runs the batches and keeps the record.</dd>
<dt>compaction</dt><dd>Step that replaces a long conversation with a short summary, so that the session can go on.</dd>
<dt>boot</dt><dd>Reading the coordinator does after every compaction, so that it knows the project again without you.</dd>
<dt>record</dt><dd>Project's memory in the repository. Here it means FACTS, POSITIONS, INDEX, PLAN and the boot note.</dd>
<dt>FACTS</dt><dd>File of what is true about Fortress and the tree, each fact with its source and its test.</dd>
<dt>POSITIONS</dt><dd>File of your decisions, each under a bold title.</dd>
<dt>INDEX</dt><dd>File with one line for each note under the explorations folder. It says where the detail is.</dd>
<dt>protocol</dt><dd>Short file of hard rules and principles for how we work together. The goal is to retire it.</dd>
<dt>boot note</dt><dd>One long line that says what is in flight right now. It is rewritten at every change.</dd>
<dt>conduct rule</dt><dd>Rule about how the coordinator works: how it talks to you, asks, decides, briefs, keeps the record and runs agents.</dd>

